Task 1: Understanding Clusters and Creating a New Cluster
Subtask 1.1: Understanding Cluster Concepts
A cluster in RHVM is a logical grouping of hosts that share the same storage domains and have the same type of CPU. Clusters provide:

• Resource pooling: Combine multiple hosts into a single resource pool • High availability: Enable VM migration between hosts • Load balancing: Distribute VMs across available hosts • Centralized management: Manage multiple hosts as a single unit

