Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Host Cannot Join Cluster
Symptoms: Host stuck in "Installing" or "Non Responsive" state

Solution:

# Check network connectivity
ping rhvh-host-01.lab.local

# Verify SSH access
ssh root@rhvh-host-01.lab.local

# Check firewall settings on host
firewall-cmd --list-all

# Restart VDSM service on host
systemctl restart vdsmd
Issue 2: Storage Domain Not Accessible
Symptoms: Storage domain shows as "Inactive"

Solution:

# Check NFS mount on host
showmount -e nfs-server.lab.local

# Test manual mount
mount -t nfs nfs-server.lab.local:/data/rhvm/data /mnt/test

# Check permissions
ls -la /data/rhvm/data
Issue 3: Network Configuration Problems
Symptoms: VMs cannot communicate or migrate fails

Solution:

# Check network configuration on host
ip addr show
ip route show

# Verify VLAN configuration
cat /proc/net/vlan/config

# Test network connectivity between hosts
ping -c 4 rhvh-host-02.lab.local
Best Practices
Cluster Design Recommendations
Naming Conventions:

Clusters: [Environment]-Cluster-[Number]
Hosts: rhvh-[cluster]-[number]
Networks: [purpose]-network-[environment]
Resource Planning: • Plan for 20% overhead on CPU and memory • Ensure adequate network bandwidth • Size storage appropriately for growth

Security Considerations: • Use separate networks for management and VM traffic • Implement proper firewall rules • Regular security updates

Monitoring and Maintenance
Regular Tasks: • Monitor resource utilization • Review event logs • Test backup and recovery procedures • Update hosts and manager regularly

Performance Optimization: • Adjust memory over-commitment based on workload • Fine-tune scheduling policies • Monitor and optimize storage performance

